    "summary": "Added the SQL reader (src/indexer/parser/sql.ts), which now owns .sql (removed from the artifact reader's extensions) behind the guarded load of @derekstride/tree-sitter-sql. It writes the artifact reader's file and document entities unchanged: same ids, names, flags, body truncation and size limit. It adds a table or view entity per CREATE TABLE / CREATE [OR REPLACE] VIEW, named by the unquoted, schema-qualified name, with DEFINES. REFERENCES go from tables to their foreign-key targets and from views to the relations they select from; the view's own CTE names are excluded and duplicates are merged. Same-file references are resolved by case-insensitive unquoted name; others stay pending by name (user decision). CREATEs inside transaction blocks and outside ERROR regions are read. New: an IndexerService SQL integration test and the twelve-languages check (ac4). Left out: other statement kinds, and DML outside views.",
